    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok got it. it's just a matter of waiting for everything to sync up. is there any other weird reason why a record might stay stale? like if there's some kind of error or something that would prevent the update from actually working?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Aside from propagation delay, there could be a few other reasons why a record might stay stale. Errors could occur with the DNS configuration, such as typos in the A record, misconfigured MX or CNAME records, or too low a TTL setting beyond just propagation delay. Also, clients might base their lookups on a local cache. To avoid such errors, always double-check your DNS configurations, ensure you have the correct IP address, and consider using a longer TTL to reduce the load on your DNS server. If problems persist, contacting your hosting provider or the host of the authoritative DNS servers may be necessary.",
      "source": "target",
